 ],
 "literal": "In the forest clearing where the yā trees were felled and burnt, / the red millet with green stems and bases resembling sugarcane, / like the broad trunk of a gentle female elephant, pouring milk, / with dense green ears of grain that have bent down like charred blocks of wood, / we will go to drive away the alighting parrots. In the forest of Malaiyan, / who has broad hands shining with spears of conquering battle, / O one with the chest fragrant with sandalwood! / Do not come here, for my mother will indeed come.",
 "translation": "In the forest clearing where the yā trees were felled and burnt, the red millet has grown with green stems as thick as sugarcane. Its ears, full of milk like the broad trunk of a gentle female elephant, have bent down like charred blocks of wood. We are going there to drive away the alighting parrots. O lord of the hills, whose chest is fragrant with sandalwood from the forests of Malaiyan, the spear-wielding warrior! Do not come here to our house, for my mother will surely come to watch over us.",
 "modern": "யா மரங்களை வெட்டிச் சுட்டுக் கரியாக்கிய காட்டின் வழியில், கரும்பைப் போன்ற அடியையுடைய பசிய தாள்களைக் கொண்ட செந்தினை வளர்ந்துள்ளது. இளைய பெண் யானையின் பெரிய துதிக்கையைப் போலப் பால் வார்ந்து, கரித்துண்டு போல வளைந்த நெருங்கிய கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட பசிய தினைப்புனத்தில் வந்து விழும் கிளிகளை ஓட்டுவதற்காக நாங்கள் செல்வோம். வெல்லும் போரில் வேல் ஏந்திய பெரிய கைகளை உடைய மலையனது காட்டிலுள்ள சந்தனம் மணக்கும் மார்பினை உடையவனே! நீ இங்கு வரவேண்டாம்; என் தாய் அங்கு வந்துவிடுவாள்.",
 "explanation": "The playmate (தோழி) is speaking to the hero (தலைவன்) who has come for a secret meeting at the heroine's house. She tells him that the red millet in the field, cleared by burning yā trees, has grown thick and ripe, its ears bending like charred wood. The heroine and her playmate are going to the field to guard it and drive away the parrots. She warns him not to come to her house because the mother is vigilant and will be there. The description of the millet field (Kuriñci landscape) with its ripe ears resembling elephant trunks and charred wood reflects the fertile mountain region. The warning serves as a subtle hint for him to seek a formal marriage rather than continuing secret trysts.",
